    "created_at": "2021-09-07T17:08:22Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-09-07T17:08:22Z",
    "body": "Yes, we're now talking about the general memory cache, which we should indeed spec, probably as a superset of the preload cache. A small first step could be to introduce this coalescing behavior to the list of available images though, and then extend that to the generalized memory cache, if we ever spec one.",
