    "created_at": "2021-09-08T06:49:24Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-09-08T06:49:24Z",
    "body": "The MemoryCache in Chromium and WebKit precedes preload, and is used to deduplicate requests for the same resource destination and same URL (with a few other constraints) regardless of preload (e.g. multiple, similar elements requesting the same resource, implicit preloading based on HTML tokenization, etc).\r\nResources in Chromium essentially go through two caches (MemoryCache and preload cache), which have slightly different rules. \r\nI'm not sure if the above is observable. Maybe it can be coalesced into a single concept, but in that case, that concept should not be a \"preload cache\", but a \"request coalesing cache\".",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
